    dct:description "As stated, the hypothesis is existential and modal rather than a concrete physical model. Existing physical data could test specified candidates but cannot confirm or refute that an unspecified program may exist. Operationalizing it would require adding content not present in the claim." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: A particular candidate program could be tested by deriving quantitative physical predictions and comparing them with observations, but the existential statement that some unspecified simple program may underlie all physics supplies no unique prediction or falsifying outcome." ;
